{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>And it came to pass on the way, at the lodging place.</b> When he went from the wilderness to Midian with his wife and sons. And this is recounted after he had fulfilled all the commandments that the blessed El had given him regarding the matter of his mission." "<b>And YHWH met him.</b> The day of his son's circumcision arrived, on which the Shekhinah rests to establish the covenant, as in the matter of נִמּוֹלוּ אִתּוֹ וַיֵּרָא אֵלָיו ה׳ (Genesis 17:23–26, 18:1). And perhaps this is the reason for the custom to prepare a Seat of Honor (כִּסֵּא כָּבוֹד) at the place of circumcision." "<b>And He sought to kill him.</b> The angel appointed over this sought to kill Moses because he had been remiss."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:24:26.086606237Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}